{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095312-will-we-ever-have-rules-for-creating-spirits","id":1095312,"title":"Will we ever have rules for creating spirits?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T18:23:56-07:00","id":1095312,"title":"Will we ever have rules for creating spirits?","content":"When Forged By Dragon's Fire cam out, I always felt that an opportunity was missed because it was probably as good a place as any, save perhaps Infinite Tapestry for the rules on creating/transforming a spirit. Is it likely that we will get the rules for doing so this time around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T18:29:49-07:00","id":1095314,"title":"","content":"I think the problem is that spirits will always be an odd place in the setting. Everything touches them so in general ST's will have their own ideas on how these things work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T04:45:03-07:00","id":1095440,"title":"","content":"I guess it is <i>possible</i> that they appear in future books...but I wouldn't bet it. HDYDT was <i>the</i> place to put that rules (the book that explains how to do things), since they didn't make it there, I don't think they will apeear in any future book <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> .<br /> <br /> But there's a lot of stuff out there that hasn't rules. This is MAGE, you use the basic rules to craft new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T08:58:52-07:00","id":1095504,"title":"","content":"I'm assuming there should be some rules related to such in the upcoming book M20: Gods, Monsters, and Familiar Strangers. I know that it will have multitudes of spirits of every stripe for use in Mage, along with other stripe of beings. If ever there was going to be a place for a section on the creation of spirits then it would be that. It's currently lavishing in 1st draft of the timeline. I know Phil is currently working on Book of the Fallen, so it may be awhile before any validation of my theory.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12563-inathicon","name":"iNathicon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T13:18:15-07:00","id":1102897,"title":"","content":"Gods and Monsters should have the rules for creating spirits, given the obvious name of the book.